Reading frontend design skill
Reading frontend design skill

Now let me plan and build this. This is a focused design tool for a mobile-first browser studio — a "consistency auditor" for icon families. Let me think through the design carefully before building.

Brief analysis: The tool needs to work as a saved HTML file on a phone. It's a professional creative utility — precise, tool-like, not decorative. The job is visual QA: define a standard, tile ~10 concepts, spot drift, copy a direction note.

Design plan:

Palette: Dark studio surface (
#0F0F11), bright inspection light (
#F5F5F0 tiles), a single drift-alert amber (
#F59E0B), and a crisp teal confirm (
#14B8A6). Not warm-cream, not acid-green — this is a QC lightbox, so the metaphor is a backlit inspection table.
Type: System monospace for labels/data (feels like a spec sheet), system sans for UI chrome. No web fonts since it's self-contained.
Layout: Sticky header with the "family DNA" panel (the standard), scrollable tile grid below, floating copy button.
Signature element: Each tile has a live "drift score" computed from deviation across 3 axes (shape, color, detail) shown as a small segmented bar — not a number, a visual diff.
Mobile-first: touch-friendly targets, single column stacking.
Created a file, read a file
Created a file, read a file

Save that file to your phone (Files app, iCloud, etc.) and open it in Safari or Chrome — it's fully self-contained, zero dependencies, and persists to localStorage so your work survives closing the tab.

What's in it:

Family DNA panel (collapsible sticky header) — define your standard: shape language, corner radius, stroke weight, fill style, detail level, optical size target, brand palette swatches, and a free-text constraints field. Everything here feeds the art direction note.

Tile grid — up to ~10 (or more) concept cards side by side. Each card has:

A tap-to-upload canvas for your icon image (PNG, SVG, JPG all work)
Three drift axes — Shape / Color / Detail — each rated Matches / Minor drift / Major drift via dropdown
A 3-segment drift bar at the bottom of the canvas that turns teal → amber → red per axis, so you can scan the grid visually without reading text
A tile observation textarea for notes
A ⚑ flag button to manually mark anything suspect, which borders the card in red
A drift badge (On-spec / Drift detected / Flagged) that updates live

Bottom bar — shows a running count of ✓ ok / ~ warn / ⚑ drift tiles. ⎘ Copy note assembles a concise art direction document — spec block, constraint list, per-tile drift flags with axis callouts, and an on-spec roster — and puts it on your clipboard ready to paste into Slack, Notion, or a brief.

Everything auto-saves to localStorage as you work, so reopening the file restores your full session.

