Here's what changed and why:

10 starter tiles, no upload. Each tile renders a CSS-drawn icon (Home, Settings, Search, Notifications, Profile, Bookmark, Analytics, Mail, Calendar, Lock) using ::before/::after pseudo-elements and child divs built by named builder functions (buildIconHome(), etc.). No <img>, no file inputs, nothing to tap or load — the grid is fully populated and comparable the instant you open the file.

Event wiring. Every handler is wired with addEventListener. The DNA inputs, swatch controls, axis selects, name fields, observation textareas, flag/delete buttons, copy button, and add-swatch button are all wired this way. There's a single small el(tag, cls) helper that calls createElement and sets className — that's the only element-creation shortcut used.

Content rendering. All user-visible text — badge labels, summary bar counts, option text, button labels — is set via textContent. The summary bar rebuilds itself by appending <span> nodes rather than templating a string. The observation textarea uses textContent for its initial value rather than .value assignment from an innerHTML source.

Persistence. On first open it seeds all 10 starters and saves to localStorage. Reload, close-and-reopen, or open on a different day — your axis ratings, names, notes, flags, and DNA spec all come back exactly as you left them.

