Good. I can see all the overflow sources without needing to guess:

html/body have no overflow-x: hidden or max-width clamp — any child that escapes its box bleeds the page.
.site-header padding 16px each side — fine on its own, but combined with the details/dna-panel border it can push out if the panel itself overflows.
.dna-grid inputs/selects — width: 100% inside a grid cell is fine, but the dna-grid itself has no min-width: 0 on cells, so grid blowout can occur.
.swatch-wrap input[type=text] is hardcoded width: 72px — fine by itself, but the flex row wraps and the ＋ button has no shrink constraint.
.bottom-bar summary text — long monospace strings with · separators have no overflow: hidden / text-overflow so they can push the copy button off screen.
.btn-copy is white-space: nowrap — correct, but it needs flex-shrink: 0 so the summary can't squash it.
CSS icon atoms use fixed px widths (44px, 40px, 38px, 36px) — at ≈185px tile width these are fine, but they have no max-width guard if the preview collapses further.
Missing min-width: 0 on flex/grid children — the single biggest silent overflow cause in both the DNA grid cells and the bottom bar flex row.
