Here's exactly what was causing the 4px bleed and what was changed to fix each one:

html and body — added overflow-x: hidden on both and max-width: 100vw on body. This is the hard backstop; any child that escapes its box gets clipped at the viewport edge rather than widening the scroll container.

.site-header — added width: 100% and overflow: hidden. A position: sticky element doesn't automatically stay within the viewport width; it needs explicit containment.

.dna-panel — added width: 100% and overflow: hidden. The panel sits inside the header's padding box; without overflow: hidden its border and children could push past it.

.dna-grid and its children — added min-width: 0 on the grid itself and .dna-grid > *. Grid cells default to min-width: auto, which means a cell's content (an input, a select) can force the cell wider than its 1fr track, blowing out the column.

DNA inputs/selects/textarea — added max-width: 100% and min-width: 0 alongside width: 100%. width: 100% alone doesn't prevent an input from reporting a minimum intrinsic width larger than its container.

.swatch-wrap input[type=text] — changed from width: 72px to width: 7ch; min-width: 0. The fixed 72px was fine in isolation but combined with the color picker and remove button it could push the row past the panel width before wrapping. 7ch scales with the font and gives the same visual result.

.tile-body, .tile-name, .tile-obs, .axis-row, .axis-sel — added min-width: 0, max-width: 100%, and display: block where needed. Cards use overflow: hidden already, but inputs inside a flex or grid child that lacks min-width: 0 can still force the parent wider before the overflow clip kicks in.

.tile-footer — added min-width: 0, overflow: hidden, and gap: 4px. The badge now has flex-shrink: 1, overflow: hidden, and text-overflow: ellipsis so it compresses rather than pushing the action buttons off-card.

.bottom-bar — added width: 100%, overflow: hidden, and box-sizing: border-box. The summary span now has min-width: 0 and overflow: hidden so its text can shrink. The copy button has flex-shrink: 0 so it's always fully visible and never squashed.

